    "why": "the digit 1 is a stray accent mark (independent svarita); read śravasyaḥ"
   }
  ],
  "notes": "johūtraḥ: an intensive formation from √hū, 'much invoked' or 'one who invokes'; the sense is uncertain. manuṣā: instrumental of manuṣ, 'by man' (or 'by Manu'); not certain. iḻaḥ pade: 'in the place of Iḷā' (Iḷā is a name; the figure is not explained here). vājī: 'prize-winner' (also 'steed, swift'). marmṛjenyaḥ: 'to be cleansed, to be adorned'. vicetāḥ with visarga dropped before m (āḥ before a voiced sound gives ā).",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
