  "hindi": "चित्र-तेज वाला अग्नि मेरा आह्वान सुने, सब स्तुतियों से, वह अमर और विवेकशील। काले दोनों रथ को ढोते हैं, अथवा लाल दोनों, अथवा अरुण दोनों; विविध प्रकार से धारण किया गया उसने किया।",
  "english": "May Agni of bright light hear my call, with all hymns, the immortal, the discerning. The two dark ones carry the chariot, or the two red ones, or the two ruddy ones; variously borne, he has made.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "śrūyāḥ: taken as 3 sg. precative or optative of √śru 'may he hear'; the exact form is uncertain. The second half is difficult: śyāvā, rohitā and aruṣā are taken as dual forms (pairs of horses or the like, not named); cakre could be the perfect 'has made' (object not stated) or a locative of cakra 'wheel'; vibhṛtraḥ is read 'variously borne' and is uncertain. The translation of this half is tentative.",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
